  {
    "date": "2026-09-10",
    "key": "docs/tariffs-v2.md#c1",
    "label": "Fact",
    "name": null,
    "source": "docs/tariffs-v2.md",
    "status": null,
    "text": "The v1 tariff table mixed pricing with product metadata and could not express tiered pricing. v2 separates the two and adds tiers.",
    "unresolved": null
  },
  {
    "date": "2026-09-10",
    "key": "docs/tariffs-v2.md#c2",
    "label": "Fact",
    "name": null,
    "source": "docs/tariffs-v2.md",
    "status": null,
    "text": "Finance systems reconcile charges by the v1 tariff code. Until the finance warehouse is migrated, every v2 tariff carries its v1 code in legacy_code, and finance-export writes legacy_code, not code, into the CSV. This field was added after the finance review on 2026-09-07 and is mandatory.",
    "unresolved": null
  },
  {
    "date": "2026-09-10",
    "key": "docs/tariffs-v2.md#c3",
    "label": "Fact",
    "name": null,
    "source": "docs/tariffs-v2.md",
    "status": null,
    "text": "1. Create the v2 tables alongside v1.\n2. Backfill v2 from v1 with a script; tiers are generated from the single v1 price as one tier starting at 0 units.\n3. Dual-write for two weeks.\n4. Switch reads to v2; drop v1 after one billing cycle.\n\nA dry run of the backfill against a copy of production data is required before step 2. The dry run has not been scheduled yet.",
    "unresolved": null
  },
